cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the manuscripts, data, or verification code in this package, cite the relevant paper and the archived software release."
title: "Distance-Antimagic Publication and Verification Package"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Waddle
    given-names: Zach
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-13
abstract: >-
  Source, compiled manuscripts, constructive and exhaustive verification code,
  full order-nine graph certificates, proof and literature audits, and
  reproducibility records for three papers on universal distance-antimagic
  labelings, exact integer and elementary-abelian-two universal classifications,
  nonlinear finite-field Cayley constructions in every dimension at least three,
  and exhaustive verification of the open-neighborhood conjecture through order nine.
keywords:
  - distance-antimagic labeling
  - graph labeling
  - group labeling
  - finite fields
  - Cayley graphs
  - Seidel switching
  - permutational sums
  - point-determining graphs
  - computational proof
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
